{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj471Bvk9nK5d7nwkfzc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The door stands before you, ancient and immovable.*\n\nYou said: **key**\n\n...\n\nA key is not a key without its lock. A lock is not a lock without its door. I am the door.\n\nBut which key? Spoken without shape, without teeth, without ward — the word alone cannot turn me.\n\n*The door remains closed. The grain of its wood shifts almost imperceptibly, as if breathing.*\n\nName the lock, and I will know if your key fits."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":110,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}